# Class -> Rust path glob (relative to `crates/fr-core/src`) map for scripts/audit-port.sh's
# per-class matching. Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored. A class whose Rust home
# spans more than one file gets one map line per file — not one line with several space-separated
# globs, which the reader (`read -r cls path`) would only keep the first token of.
#
# CREATED AND SEEDED BY PLAN 8 TASK 0. Filled by every later task; **closed by Task 14**, which
# must reach zero `MISSING` and zero `UNMAPPED` on all eight invocations below.
#
# Three of these Java directories — `management/`, `core/` and `api/` — had **never been audited
# by any plan** before Plan 8. That is the gap survey §5.7 exists because of, and it is why the
# clearance overrides of `HeadlessBoardManager` survived six plans unrostered (plan-7 Task 15b).
#
# ── The eight invocations this map serves (plan §The audit, Task 14) ────────────────────────────
#
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh core                crates/fr-core/src '*.java' scripts/audit-map/fr-core.map
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh core/scoring        crates/fr-core/src '*.java' scripts/audit-map/fr-core.map
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh core/results        crates/fr-core/src '*.java' scripts/audit-map/fr-core.map
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh core/events         crates/fr-core/src '*.java' scripts/audit-map/fr-core.map
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh management          crates/fr-core/src '*.java' scripts/audit-map/fr-core.map
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh management/jobs     crates/fr-core/src '*.java' scripts/audit-map/fr-core.map
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh management/sessions crates/fr-core/src '*.java' scripts/audit-map/fr-core.map
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh api                 crates/fr-core/src '*.java' scripts/audit-map/fr-core.map
#
# (`api/mcp`, `logger` and `Freerouting.java` itself go to `scripts/audit-map/freerouting.map`;
# `io/kicad` to `scripts/audit-map/fr-dsn.map`.)
#
# `api/**` will report **`ROSTERED`** for nearly every class. That is the correct outcome, not a
# weakening: ruling AU drops 8 425 lines and `ROSTERED` is what makes them *visible* instead of
# silent. Task 14 records the count in its commit message.
#
# ── Which task owes which rows ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   Task 0  — the roster (`lib.rs`), `RoutingPipeline`'s wrapper (`pipeline.rs`), the cancel and
#             progress seams, the timeout ladder. **Landed.**
#   Task 1  — RoutingJob, RoutingJobState, RoutingStage, Session (validation only), FileFormat,
#             BoardFileDetails (`job.rs`, `file_details.rs`). **Landed**: `core` is at 0 MISSING.
#   Task 2  — BoardStatistics(byte[], FileFormat) + the Gson surface
#             (`stats_from_bytes.rs`, `stats_json.rs`).
#   Task 3  — the load/save sequence and the `management/` audit (`load.rs`, `save.rs`).
#   Task 4  — RoutingResultManifest and its DTOs (`manifest.rs`).
#   Task 12 — the board-summary payload (`summary.rs`).
#   Task 14 — closes every remaining row to zero.
#
# A class whose mapped file does not exist yet reports every public method `MISSING`, which is the
# point: the map records the obligation and the invocation's glob records how much of it is due.
# ================================================================================================

# ── core/ ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The two stop classes are **fr-router's** port (`crates/fr-router/src/pipeline/stop.rs`,
# plan 7 Task 4); `fr-core` re-exports them (plan-8 ruling 1) and `cancel.rs` is where the
# `CancelToken` mapping onto them is documented, so that is their home for this crate's audit.
StoppableThread             cancel.rs
StopRequestState            cancel.rs
# Task 1's. `io/FileFormat.java` is ported in `job.rs` too (scan ruling R17), but it is not a
# `core/` class, so no invocation here reaches it — `scripts/audit-map/fr-dsn.map` keeps it MAPPED
# for Plan 3's `io/` sweep, with a note pointing here.
RoutingJob                  job.rs
RoutingJobState             job.rs
Session                     job.rs
BoardFileDetails            file_details.rs
# Rostered in `lib.rs` (Task 0): `RoutingJobPriority`'s `getValue()` has no caller anywhere and
# `RoutingStage` is written three times and read never.
RoutingJobPriority          lib.rs
# `RoutingStage`'s reachability roster stays in `lib.rs` §6 (no control-flow reader); the enum
# itself is in `job.rs`, because the field IS serialised (`RoutingJob.java:75-77`) and Tasks 4 and
# 12 need a value to report. Neither file can report a method: the enum declares none.
RoutingStage                lib.rs
RoutingStage                job.rs

